{
 "item": "1.29 Bash edit diff (2026-09-13): a Bash result's bashEditDiff sidecar draws one resolved edit card per changed file under the Bash line, after its IN/OUT box; a file-count cap and moreFiles surface as a note; live and replay share appendBashDiff",
 "branch": "onClaudeEvent user/tool_result -> onUserEvent (75-retraction.js) reads ev.tool_use_result.bashEditDiff -> appendBashDiff (50-blocks.js: fillAppliedCard per file, patchRows over the CLI's hunks, noteLine for hidden files) after t.io; replay: SessionStore.applyToolResult copies toolUseResult.bashEditDiff to item.bashDiff -> renderBlocks 'tool' (55-replay.js) -> the same appendBashDiff",
 "provenance": "Step 1's user frame is the REAL 2.1.270 record from the 2026-09-13 stdio probe (tools/probe_stdio.py, one `printf 'probe line\\n' >> probe_bash_diff.txt` turn in the testing repo; tape in the 2026-09-13 session scratchpad cli/bashdiff.jsonl): content '(Bash completed with no output)', tool_use_result {stdout, stderr, interrupted, isImage, noOutputExpected, bashEditDiff{files:[{filePath, hunks:[{oldStart:0, oldLines:0, newStart:1, newLines:1, lines:['+probe line']}], created:true}], moreFiles:0, changedFiles}} - note the LIVE frame carries the sidecar as snake-case `tool_use_result` (the 2026-08-05 'live carries no toolUseResult' note is out of date at 2.1.270). Steps 2-4 EXTEND that shape (an edit hunk with - and +, two files, moreFiles>0, twelve files, is_error:true) - those combinations were NOT observed on the wire; they prove our own capping and error paths, nothing about the CLI. Step 5 feeds our replay JSON (`bashDiff` as SessionStore serialises it) through renderBlocks - self-consistency of the two paths, pinned by SessionStoreTest on the Kotlin side. Step 6 is the pre-existing no-sidecar path (control). NEGATIVE CONTROL RUN 2026-09-13 against the pre-change build (0.13.1 sources in the sandbox; fixture written first): 22 of 27 asserts FAILED, every one on a discriminating case (0 cards, no header, no rows, no footer, no note in steps 1-5); the 5 that passed guard the untouched paths — the IN+OUT rows in step 1, the no-note case, the red dot in step 4, and both step-6 control asserts. POST-BUILD, REAL PANEL 2026-09-13 (sandbox, real CLI 2.1.270, testing repo): a first turn in plan→manual mode drew NO card — the CLI attaches bashEditDiff only in auto/bypassPermissions by default (three more stdio probes: --mode default none, --mode acceptEdits none, --mode default + user settings bashEditDiffEnabled:true present; the step-1 probe had come up in auto, which is why it carried one). The same turn in auto mode drew 'Bash on live_probe.txt' / '+ live probe line' / ✓ Applied under the IN/OUT box (screenshot live_1_29.png in that session's scratchpad). Fixture 87 on the new build: 27/27; full harness 856/0.",
